    {
      "id": 19860,
      "nameEs": "Ghouls 'n Ghosts",
      "originalName": "Ghouls 'n Ghosts",
      "year": 1988,
      "igdbId": 6817,
      "popularity": 77,
      "iconic": false,
      "fields": [
        {
          "field": "best_version",
          "value": "49831",
          "source": "claude",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "name_es",
          "value": "Ghouls 'n Ghosts",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "original_name",
          "value": "Ghouls 'n Ghosts",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "summary",
          "value": "The gameplay for Ghouls 'n Ghosts is similar to that of Ghosts 'n Goblins. The player controls the knight Arthur, who must advance through a series of eerie levels and defeat a number of undead and demonic creatures in his quest to restore the souls stolen by Lucifer (Loki in the English-language Mega Drive and Sega Master System versions), including the soul of his lover, Princess Prin Prin. Along the way, Arthur can pick up a variety of weapons and armor to help him in his quest. While the core gameplay remains the same as its predecessor, the game now allows Arthur to fire directly upward and directly downward while in mid air.\n\nBy jumping in certain spots, players can cause a treasure chest to erupt from the ground. By firing his weapon at the chest, players may uncover new weapons, gold armor or an evil magician that changes Arthur into an elderly man or a helpless duck. The gold armor allows players to charge up the weapon to release a powerful magical attack. Each weapon has its own special attack.\n\nThere are five levels and Lucifer's chamber at the end, considered a sixth level in itself. To defeat the game, Arthur must complete level 1 to 5 twice. Upon completing level's 1 to 5 the first time, Arthur is taken back to level 1 again but this time a special weapon appears during the game. To enter Lucifer's chamber the player must have this special weapon equipped and defeat the penultimate boss.",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "summary_es",
          "value": "La jugabilidad de Ghouls 'n Ghosts es similar a la de Ghosts 'n Goblins. El jugador controla al caballero Arthur, que debe avanzar por una serie de niveles espeluznantes y derrotar a varias criaturas no muertas y demoníacas en su misión de restaurar las almas robadas por Lucifer (Loki en las versiones en inglés para Mega Drive y Sega Master System), incluida el alma de su amada, la princesa Prin Prin. En el camino, Arthur puede recoger una variedad de armas y armaduras que le ayudarán en su misión. Aunque la jugabilidad básica se mantiene igual que en su predecesor, ahora Arthur puede disparar directamente hacia arriba y hacia abajo mientras está en el aire.\n\nSaltando en ciertos puntos, los jugadores pueden hacer que surja del suelo un cofre del tesoro. Al disparar al cofre, pueden descubrir nuevas armas, armadura dorada o un mago malvado que convierte a Arthur en un anciano o en un pato indefenso. La armadura dorada permite cargar el arma para lanzar un poderoso ataque mágico. Cada arma tiene su propio ataque especial.\n\nHay cinco niveles y, al final, la cámara de Lucifer, considerada en sí misma un sexto nivel. Para derrotar el juego, Arthur debe completar los niveles 1 a 5 dos veces. Al completar los niveles 1 a 5 por primera vez, Arthur vuelve al nivel 1, pero esta vez aparece un arma especial durante el juego. Para entrar en la cámara de Lucifer, el jugador debe tener equipada esta arma especial y derrotar al penúltimo jefe.",
          "source": "claude",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "year",
          "value": "1988",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        }
      ],
